A||||8||Coupe'N||suspension info needed inside...||||5||
Z||000000||Coupe'N||06-16-2001||07:51 PM||||Hey everyone, I am getting rid of my 84 SE parts car this week. It came with the WS6 suspension which is not on my 87 coupe. I have looked up the RPO codes and my 84 has the stiffest WS6 springs. How hard is it to get the springs swapped, and are they even interchangable??<BR>Thanks for any info/input.<P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||06-16-2001||08:07 PM||||You can interchange anything on the suspensions of '84-'87 models.<P>To swap springs you just need to loosen/remove the lower control arm (I just pop the lower balljoint out of the spindle and remove it that way).<P>The rears can be removed with the struts as a unit.  If the struts are in good shape you can just install them on your '87, otherwise you'll have to disassemble the strut assembly (not hard to do).<P>LMK if you need any help......I'll e-mail you better instructions.  This is by no means a difficult job, but you'll obviously need some tools.  I think a shop would charge an arm and/or a leg to do this, so doing it yourself would be the best bet.<P>Good luck! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-16-2001||09:20 PM||||At the very least... save the parts for later. If you don't use them someone else will. Don't forget to record the spring codes from the label in the car...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coupe'N||06-16-2001||10:30 PM||||Thanks guys... THIS FORUM IS QUICK WITH THE REPLIES  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  mrfiero would you go ahead and email those instructions you mentioned. <BR>Thanks again.<P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||06-16-2001||11:37 PM||||No problem......I'll e-mail you later tonight.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Coupe'N||06-17-2001||03:32 PM||||Just wanted to say thanks for the email mrfiero. I will take a stab at this project this week. I have some spring compressors at my grandparents house that I have to pick up later today. Plus my tools are at work. I'lll let you all know if I have any problems.<P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||06-17-2001||04:29 PM||||How do you know which susp. package the car came with?  Like ws6 or not? I have an 84 SE, it has the 14" alum. wheels.  Not sure if that matters any... ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Coupe'N||06-17-2001||05:21 PM||||Check your RPO codes under your hood. The WS6 package is actually listed as "WS6" I believe it consists of the front and rear springs, and a larger front sway bar. There are a couple online services guides that have the description of the RPO codes. You can find out what options you have on your fiero by looking cross refrencing the two.<P>Just look under your hood and look for the "WS6" rpo code, if you see it, you have it. If you don't see WS6, you probably have the regular style suspension under there.<BR>Let me know what you find!<P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||6
Z||000008||Songman||06-17-2001||05:50 PM||||Here is a cool page of RPO codes someone created...<BR> <A HREF="http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/RPOlist.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/RPOlist.html</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
